      "text": "method. Given the negatively-charged nature of major PFAS molecules at neutral pH, two types of anion-exchange moieties, tertiary-amine (TA) and quaternary ammonium (QA), were chemically grafted to the membrane backbone materials. PFOA and PFOS were selected as representative PFAS molecules. The major objectives of the study were summarized as: (1) development of durable adsorptive membranes with both high permeability and effective PFAS removal; (2) evaluation of the roles of hydrophobic membrane backbone and ion-exchange moiety on removal mechanisms; (3) investigation of long-term removal perfor - mance and membrane stability; and (4) establishment of a pH-swing strategy towards PFOA adsorption and facile membrane regeneration. 2. Material and methods 2.1. Materials The PET nonwoven fabric was ordered from Iris International Trading Co., Ltd., while PVDF powder (M w ~ 300,000), 2-(dimethyla - mino)ethyl methacrylate (referred to as TA agent), [2-(meth - acryloyloxy)ethyl]trimethylammonium chloride (referred to as QA agent), and dimethylformamide (DMF), and bovine serum albumin (BSA) were obtained from Sigma-Aldrich. Sodium persulfate, fulvic acid, sodium alginate, inorganic salts, as well as feedstocks and analytical"
